===Etymology 3===
{{ety|en|:lbor|la:-a<id:nominal>|id=feminine}}
{{lbor|en|la|-a|pos=nominative [[Appendix:Latin first declension|first declension neuter]] singular suffix}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|ə|a=RP,GenAm}}, {{IPA|en|/ə/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|en|suffix|plural|-as|or|-ae}}

# {{n-g|Marks singular nouns, with a foundation in [[Greek]] or [[Latin]], often implying femininity, especially when contrasted with words terminating in {{m|en|-us}}.}}
# {{n-g|Changes an [[element]] or substance into an [[oxide]].}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|magnesium|magnesia}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|feminine suffix}} {{l|en|-ess}}, {{l|en|-ette}}, {{l|en|-ine}}, {{l|en|-ress}}, {{l|en|she-}}, {{l|en|-trix}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{antsense|feminine suffix}} {{l|en|he-}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|incuba}}

===Etymology 4===
{{ety|en|:bor|it:-a|es:-a<id:feminine>|pt:-a|text=+|dot=,|id=feminine}} all {{lg|feminine}} noun suffixes from {{der|en|la|-a}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ə/|a=RP,GenAm}}

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix}}

# {{n-g|Marks nouns, with a foundation in [[Italian]], [[Spanish]], or [[Portuguese]], implying femininity.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[donna|donn'''a''']]}}
#: {{ux|en|[[signora|signor'''a''']]}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|female suffix}} {{l|en|-ess}}, {{l|en|-ette}}, {{l|en|-ine}}, {{l|en|-ress}}, {{l|en|she-}}, {{l|en|-trix}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{antsense|female suffix}} {{l|en|he-}}

===Etymology 5===
{{ety|en|id=music}}
Added especially for [[metrical]] reasons, or as an empty filler syllable.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ə/|/eɪ/|a=RP,GenAm}}

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix}}

# {{n-g|Added for [[metrical]] reasons to songs, poetry and verse, or as an empty filler syllable to other speech.}}
#: {{alti|en|a|a-}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|IV|iii|text=A merry heart goes all the day<br>Your sad tires in a mile-'''a'''}}
#* '''1936''' July 18, {{w|Leon Schlesinger}} (producer) / {{w|Norman Spencer}} (music), ''{{w|I Love to Singa}}'':
#*: I love to sing'''-a''' / about the moon'''-a''' and the June'''-a''' and the spring'''-a''', / I love to sing'''-a''' / about a sky of blue'''-a''', or a tea for two'''-a'''.
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1981|author= Colin Hay, Ron Strykert, performed by Men At Work|title=Down Under|passage=Buying bread from a man in Brussels <br>He was six-foot-four and full of muscle <br>I said, "Do you speak-'''a''' my language?" <br>He just smiled and gave me a Vegemite sandwich {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Don Pendleton|title=California Hit|publisher=Open Road Media|isbn=9781497685642
|passage="I'm-a tell'''-a''' you why you better be. I named you in my will, Franco."}}

